{"id":"000VLU","title":"Two sides of a ratio","author":"Ollos","solvedCount":2,"difficulty":1,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-10-19T10:52:14+00:00","posted":"Heute, 11:53 Uhr","rules":"Normal sudoku rules apply.\n\nPlace the digits 1-9 in every row, column and 3x3 box.\n\nRatio kropki dots:\n\nDigits connected by a black dot are of 1:2 ratio with one another.\n\nIkpork dots:\n\nDigits connected by a pink ikpork dot must individually be able to appear on either side of a valid ratio kropki dot (for a 9x9), but the two digits must not be in a 1:2 ratio.\n\n(Example: with \"1-2-4-8-3-6\", 2 cannot connect to 1 and 4 due to being in 1:2 ratio with both)\n\nConsecutive kropki dots:\n\nDigits connected by a white dot are consecutive.","solutionCode":"Row 9","tags":["Sudoku","Kropki"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/78zvar99wb","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/78zvar99wb","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["overlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-10-19T10:52:14+00:00"}